<title>FRANCE: Thomson-CSF rises on auction report.</title>
<headline>Thomson-CSF rises on auction report.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in state-controlled defence group Thomson-CSF gained 2.5 percent to 173.50 francs at 1005 GMT on reports the government plans to call an auction among qualified bidders for its 60 percent stake.</p>
<p>A Finance Ministry official said a decision had not yet been taken.</p>
<p>&quot;We are still studying the advantages and inconveniences of a flotation and a private placement,&quot; the official said. &quot;No decision has yet been taken,&quot; she added.</p>
<p>Newspaper Les Echos reported this morning the Finance Ministry was planning an auction for the stake.</p>
</text>
